# Copy this file to .env and fill it in. .env is gitignored -- never commit it.
#
# docker compose reads .env from this folder automatically, and run_all.bat
# loads it before starting anything, so this one file configures both the
# Docker and the native (Windows) way of running the app.

# ── ShaktiDB (PostgreSQL) superuser password ─────────────────────────────────
# Read by the Postgres container AND by the app, so both sides see one value.
#
#   NEW INSTALL      Choose a strong, unique password. Postgres sets it when it
#                    first initialises its data volume.
#
#   EXISTING INSTALL Set this to the password your database was CREATED with.
#                    Postgres only reads POSTGRES_PASSWORD on first
#                    initialisation, so changing this line later does NOT change
#                    the database's password. To rotate it: connect, run
#                        ALTER USER postgres PASSWORD 'new-password';
#                    then put the new value here and restart.
#
# Left empty, docker compose refuses to start with a message naming this
# variable, and a native run falls back to the local SQLite database instead of
# your data.
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=
